            "typeName": "dataSources",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": [
              "Printed primary source. N. De Pauw (ed.), De voorgeboden der stad Gent in de XIVe eeuw (1337-1382), Gent Arnoot-Braeckman, 1885. What we call here “public health related ordinances” are ordinances which deal with the following topics: circulation, public sanitation, trade and market regulations, zoning of crafts, immoral behaviours, animals, water management and fire safety."
            ]
          }
